  "details": "Instance: id, name, type (public/invite/etc.), owner, status, player count, capacity, restrictions (age-gate and blocked features). World: id, name, tags, which favorite list it is in (if it is favorited by the user).\n\nFor privacy, some of these might be behind a setting (like the head and wrist tracking data). Additionally, you can make the setting only show up when requested via OSCQuery to avoid bloating the settings menu.\n\nThese are possible to get from the logs and the API but you need to run a program on the same device or have to handle auth. Sending these over OSC would make making some cross-platform and cross-device OSC programs simpler, and more convenient for users to use.\n\nFor me, world id and instance type are the most important.",
